# Laptop CPU floor

Idle CPU must stay at **10% or higher** on this Mac. 0% idle freezes Cursor. Before any heavy command, run `cd backend && npm run cpu`. If `"ok": false`, do not start more work.

Parallelize tool calls and crawl workers, but never stack catalog jobs. One crawl at a time. Crawls already pause when idle dips and kill Playwright Chrome below 5% idle. Do not fight that by launching more processes.

Never start:

- `npm run pipeline` / `scripts/pipeline.mts`
- `discover` with no state/province filter
- a second photos/structure/enrich/hours/promo/screen job while one is running

Never set `OUTSET_ALLOW_CRAWL`. If headless Chrome is already running: `cd backend && npm run chrome:reap`. Leave Cursor Helper and Google Chrome.app alone.

Catalog-scale crawls belong on Render (`outset-pipeline`).
